.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt MMAP 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm mmap ,
.Nm munmap ,
.Nm mprotect ,
.Nm madvise ,
.Nm mincore
.Nd map and protect memory
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/mman.h
.Ft void *
.Fn mmap "void *address" "size_t length" "int protection" "int flags" "int fd" "off_t offset"
.Ft int
.Fn munmap "void *address" "size_t length"
.Ft int
.Fn mprotect "void *address" "size_t length" "int protection"
.Ft int
.Fn madvise "void *address" "size_t length" "int advice"
.Ft int
.Fn mincore "void *address" "size_t length" "unsigned char *vector"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The memory-mapping family creates, removes and changes virtual-memory mappings. .Fn mincore
reports residency; .Fn madvise supplies usage advice.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn mmap returns the mapping address or .Dv MAP_FAILED. The other functions return 0 or -1.
.Sh ERRORS
.Er EINVAL is returned for an invalid length or advice. .Er ENOMEM is returned when the
mapping cannot be created. .Er EACCES is returned for a protection conflict.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libc 7
.Sh STANDARDS
POSIX.1-2024; ring 0.
.Sh CAVEATS
MAP_FIXED replaces an existing mapping.
Unsupported .Fn madvise advice is ignored.
.Fn mincore reports the mappings the kernel can inspect.
See document 08 and document 11.
